From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] arm64: dts: qcom: Add Oculus Quest 2 (hollywood)

Add the device tree for the Oculus Quest 2 (Qualcomm XR2 / SM8250).

Linux is started from Android by kexec, using the quest-kexec boot
loader (https://github.com/Mac898/quest-kexec), and much of the
hardware is still in use by Android, the secure world and the remote
processors. Only what this port drives is enabled: CPUs with cpufreq-hw
and thermal trips, the fan and status LED, USB 2.0 peripheral, the
battery gauge (read-only), the syncboss MCU, the warm reset, the apps
SMMU in inherit mode, and the headless GPU nodes. The rest, including
UFS, display, remote processors and the charger, is disabled, and
unused TLMM pins are reserved.

Signed-off-by: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
